Here it comes!

254
00:14:23,780 --> 00:14:27,317
Everyone, when you're done, go ahead
and put your wet clothes in here.

255
00:14:27,400 --> 00:14:28,240
Yes, ma 'am!

256
00:14:29,460 --> 00:14:31,260
Whoa, look at that.

257
00:14:31,520 --> 00:14:33,880
It's washing all our clothes. Well,

258
00:14:34,120 --> 00:14:38,944
I never expected Boxo could do the laundry,
Magic items these days sure are handy.

259
00:14:39,140 --> 00:14:40,375
Let's go take a bath.

260
00:14:40,540 --> 00:14:43,197
He should be done washing
everything by the time we get out.

261
00:14:43,280 --> 00:14:44,110
Aww.

262
00:14:44,920 --> 00:14:49,580
You guys better make it snappy, or
the licking monster will catch you!

263
00:14:50,240 --> 00:14:51,720
Don't run away from you!

264
00:14:52,780 --> 00:14:54,015
What are we gonna do?

265
00:14:54,240 --> 00:14:56,181
There's no hot water in the bath.

266
00:14:56,540 --> 00:14:58,617
Goodness, that's certainly not ideal.

267
00:14:58,700 --> 00:15:01,171
Who was supposed to be on bath duty today?

268
00:15:02,340 --> 00:15:04,437
We're really sorry about this, ma 'am.

269
00:15:04,520 --> 00:15:06,197
We were having so much
fun playing with you.

270
00:15:06,280 --> 00:15:07,809
Shibby, we totally forgot.

271
00:15:08,120 --> 00:15:08,980
I see now.

272
00:15:09,180 --> 00:15:10,437
It's good you told me.

273
00:15:10,520 --> 00:15:11,520
Thank you, girls.

274
00:15:11,940 --> 00:15:15,764
Remember, everybody makes mistakes,
but we shouldn't cover it up.

275
00:15:16,100 --> 00:15:19,597
Instead, we should always take
responsibility for them and learn from it.

276
00:15:19,680 --> 00:15:20,510
Okay.

277
00:15:21,080 --> 00:15:25,137
By the time we gather the water and
wood to heat it up, it'll be too late.

278
00:15:25,220 --> 00:15:27,455
Why don't we skip the baths for today?

279
00:15:27,540 --> 00:15:30,187
We'll make sure we wash
up properly tomorrow.

280
00:15:32,080 --> 00:15:33,040
Huh? Voxo?

281
00:15:33,560 --> 00:15:34,397
What's going on?

282
00:15:34,480 --> 00:15:35,657
I've never seen that before.

283
00:15:35,740 --> 00:15:38,260
Behold, my fourth form change of the day.

284
00:15:38,560 --> 00:15:40,977
I've turned into a hot
spring vending machine.

285
00:15:41,060 --> 00:15:42,317
What are you planning?

286
00:15:42,400 --> 00:15:45,165
Is something supposed to
come out of this hose?

287
00:15:45,900 --> 00:15:47,280
Whoa, look at it go!

288
00:15:47,700 --> 00:15:49,680
The tub is full of water already!

289
00:15:50,460 --> 00:15:51,820
Waxo is amazing!

290
00:15:52,600 --> 00:15:53,600
Let's go!

291
00:15:54,340 --> 00:15:55,580
Hey, wait for me!

292
00:15:57,200 --> 00:15:58,030
Stop!

293
00:15:58,200 --> 00:15:59,376
Don't run, you guys!

294
00:16:15,820 --> 00:16:17,060
Thank you, Boxo.

295
00:16:17,240 --> 00:16:19,517
We appreciate everything
you've done for us.

296
00:16:19,600 --> 00:16:20,430
Hello there.

297
00:16:20,660 --> 00:16:21,954
To be honest with you,

298
00:16:22,080 --> 00:16:26,197
whenever Shui would come home, it seemed
like she was worried about something.

299
00:16:26,280 --> 00:16:28,986
It's a relief to see her
so happy and relaxed.

300
00:16:29,100 --> 00:16:31,277
That's in no small part thanks to you.

301
00:16:31,360 --> 00:16:33,237
I hope you'll continue to look after her.

302
00:16:33,320 --> 00:16:34,150
Hello there.

303
00:16:43,200 --> 00:16:47,494
I might as well give them a couple
extra sets of clothes and towels, too.

304
00:16:48,420 --> 00:16:49,250
Hold on.

305
00:16:49,333 --> 00:16:53,057
Maybe I'm overthinking it, but am I
just teaching them to expect handouts?

306
00:16:53,140 --> 00:16:56,728
I'm never sure how involved I
should get in these situations.

307
00:16:57,440 --> 00:16:59,837
Hey, Foxo, your lights started flickering.

308
00:16:59,920 --> 00:17:03,391
You weren't thinking about
something weird again, were you?

309
00:17:04,560 --> 00:17:05,390
Aw, crap.

310
00:17:05,473 --> 00:17:08,577
Apparently I do that involuntarily
when I'm lost in thought.

311
00:17:08,660 --> 00:17:10,954
You really should have more confidence.

312
00:17:11,180 --> 00:17:13,997
Everyone here is smiling
because of all the good food.

313
00:17:14,080 --> 00:17:16,420
And that's thanks to you. So be happy.

314
00:17:17,940 --> 00:17:19,140
Lamas is amazing.

315
00:17:19,560 --> 00:17:22,117
She can tell what a vending
machine like me is feeling,

316
00:17:22,200 --> 00:17:24,788
and then she knows the
perfect thing to say.

317
00:17:25,920 --> 00:17:29,760
Every day I count my lucky stars
it was Lamas who first found me.

318
00:17:36,340 --> 00:17:39,222
We're in a cave where you
can't even see the sky.

319
00:17:39,560 --> 00:17:42,501
It's nearly impossible to
tell morning from night.

320
00:17:43,600 --> 00:17:46,560
Boxo, thanks for everything
that you did today.

321
00:17:46,920 --> 00:17:49,979
It's been a while since
I've seen everyone so happy.

322
00:17:50,120 --> 00:17:51,296
Thank you very much!

323
00:17:52,820 --> 00:17:55,349
Giving all that away
must have been pricey.

324
00:17:55,860 --> 00:17:57,742
I'll make it up to you, I swear.

325
00:17:57,980 --> 00:17:59,509
I just need a little time.

326
00:18:00,520 --> 00:18:01,477
Too bad. Huh?

327
00:18:01,560 --> 00:18:04,377
Oh, you want your money now, too bad?

328
00:18:04,460 --> 00:18:05,917
Thank you very much.

329
00:18:06,000 --> 00:18:09,257
Wait, what do you mean?

330
00:18:09,340 --> 00:18:11,477
Are you saying I don't
need to pay you back?

331
00:18:11,560 --> 00:18:12,737
Hello there!

332
00:18:12,820 --> 00:18:19,457
I was kind of thirsty,

333
00:18:19,540 --> 00:18:20,617
so this is perfect.

334
00:18:20,700 --> 00:18:23,797
Wait, don't chug it like that.

335
00:18:23,880 --> 00:18:27,857
You could even win a reward.

336
00:18:27,940 --> 00:18:32,477
Anyway, this is your
first time here, right?

337
00:18:32,560 --> 00:18:36,717
Did you know everyone entering the dungeon
has to pass through the origin stratum?

338
00:18:36,800 --> 00:18:40,377
Too bad to get to the other strata?

339
00:18:40,460 --> 00:18:43,217
Adventurers have to make their
way through this stratum first,

340
00:18:43,300 --> 00:18:45,557
and then they take the
transfer circle out.

341
00:18:45,640 --> 00:18:46,470
It's a test.

342
00:18:46,553 --> 00:18:50,977
If somebody can't handle the journey through
the origin stratum, then it's a sign?

343
00:18:51,060 --> 00:18:53,997
and they have no business trying
to go deeper into the dungeon.

344
00:18:54,080 --> 00:18:54,910
Hold on.

345
00:18:54,993 --> 00:18:57,137
You're saying that all
the non-hunters I've met

346
00:18:57,220 --> 00:18:59,517
so far have had to make
their way through this place?

347
00:18:59,600 --> 00:19:03,257
But because of that, there are a
lot of people left in the stratum?

348
00:19:03,340 --> 00:19:07,037
who, for whatever reason, never
made it to the transfer circle.

349
00:19:07,120 --> 00:19:09,937
This is where the children
who were abandoned gather,

350
00:19:10,020 --> 00:19:12,157
stuck in a place where they
can't even see the sun?

351
00:19:12,240 --> 00:19:14,122
or feel the wind on their faces.

352
00:19:14,380 --> 00:19:15,615
They're trapped here.

353
00:19:17,600 --> 00:19:21,071
All I want is for the children
in this stratum to be happy.

354
00:19:21,580 --> 00:19:22,410
Sorry.

355
00:19:22,493 --> 00:19:25,177
For some reason, I've been
a real blabbermouth today.

356
00:19:25,260 --> 00:19:28,060
Forget everything I
said, okay? It's bedtime!

357
00:19:28,520 --> 00:19:29,814
I'll see you tomorrow!

358
00:19:35,840 --> 00:19:37,520
So where is this place?

359
00:19:37,740 --> 00:19:39,211
We're almost there, boss.

360
00:19:39,580 --> 00:19:42,317
Heard they've got some
kind of special magic item.

361
00:19:42,400 --> 00:19:45,277
It's been a while since
anyone's tried to steal me.

362
00:19:45,360 --> 00:19:49,417
I guess I should have expected this
since this area isn't exactly safe.

363
00:19:49,500 --> 00:19:52,937
You're saying this giant box
spits out as much food as we want?

364
00:19:53,020 --> 00:19:54,920
I saw it with my own eyes, sir.

365
00:19:56,000 --> 00:19:57,300
What should I do here?

366
00:19:57,560 --> 00:20:00,177
I could wake up Lamas and
Shwee with a loud noise.

367
00:20:00,260 --> 00:20:03,907
But if things go south, the kids
could be put into harm's way.

368
00:20:04,100 --> 00:20:04,930
All right.

369
00:20:05,700 --> 00:20:09,700
I hope you jerks are ready for this
week's vending machine surprise.

370
00:20:09,820 --> 00:20:10,650
The hell?

371
00:20:10,760 --> 00:20:12,117
Where's the smoke coming from?

372
00:20:12,200 --> 00:20:14,340
Also, is anyone else hearing that?

373
00:20:17,000 --> 00:20:20,777
Yeah, it kind of sounds like flowing water
and howling wind, but that can be like...

374
00:20:20,860 --> 00:20:21,690
What are you talking about?

375
00:20:21,773 --> 00:20:23,817
There aren't any rivers
or springs around here.

376
00:20:23,900 --> 00:20:25,606
You must be imagining things.

377
00:20:26,400 --> 00:20:28,120
And finally, the burial.

378
00:20:31,060 --> 00:20:32,080
Run, dammit!

379
00:20:32,240 --> 00:20:34,240
We gotta get the hell out of here!

380
00:20:34,460 --> 00:20:36,380
Please wait for us, boss.

381
00:20:37,980 --> 00:20:38,810
Too bad.

382
00:20:39,140 --> 00:20:41,258
I look forward to serving you again.

383
00:20:44,720 --> 00:20:47,426
Did this really happen
while we were sleeping?

384
00:20:47,660 --> 00:20:48,900
I recognize them.

385
00:20:49,100 --> 00:20:52,497
They're a couple of former
hunters who set up a base nearby.

386
00:20:52,580 --> 00:20:54,540
So they turn to a life of crime.

387
00:20:55,320 --> 00:20:56,680
Such naughty boys.

388
00:20:59,060 --> 00:20:59,890
All right.

389
00:21:00,260 --> 00:21:02,142
I'll be heading out for a while.

390
00:21:03,440 --> 00:21:05,817
Can you two look after
the children for me?

391
00:21:05,900 --> 00:21:06,780
Yes, ma 'am.

392
00:21:10,640 --> 00:21:14,464
It's been forever since I've seen
her actually get mad like this.

393
00:21:15,540 --> 00:21:18,397
Madam Director's the person
who taught me archery.

394
00:21:18,480 --> 00:21:19,892
She used to be a hunter.

395
00:21:20,400 --> 00:21:24,337
Apparently she and Director Bear used
to go raiding together all the time.

396
00:21:24,420 --> 00:21:27,714
Even Captain Kerioyl admits
she's a lot better than him.

397
00:21:27,800 --> 00:21:29,240
Oh, I didn't know that.

398
00:21:31,120 --> 00:21:35,740
About an hour later, she returned
with a big smile on her face.

399
00:21:36,020 --> 00:21:37,079
Everything's fine.

400
00:21:37,220 --> 00:21:40,977
I gave them a stern talking to, and they
were more than happy to listen to reason.

401
00:21:41,060 --> 00:21:44,648
They promised that they'd never
try to meddle with you again.

402
00:21:44,940 --> 00:21:48,557
I'm pretty sure that quiver was full
of arrows when she left earlier.

403
00:21:48,640 --> 00:21:50,380
Thank you very much.

404
00:21:51,500 --> 00:21:53,037
That's Shwee's teacher for you.

405
00:21:53,120 --> 00:21:54,357
Hold on a second.

406
00:21:54,440 --> 00:21:58,616
Does that mean Shwee's gonna grow up
to be like Madam Director one day?

407
00:22:00,420 --> 00:22:01,361
Something wrong?

408
00:22:01,880 --> 00:22:02,860
Too bad

409
00:22:19,820 --> 00:22:20,650
I'll

410
00:22:42,420 --> 00:22:46,420
I love you, but I'm
happy with this moment.

411
00:22:49,960 --> 00:22:54,960
Today is a day for a
day, always for a soup.

412
00:23:34,660 --> 00:23:39,120
I look forward to serving you again.
